# Netlify _redirects for executionpointconsulting.com
# Canonical domain: executionpointconsulting.com (non-www)
# Your live pages are already clean URLs. These rules 301 the old .html
# duplicates to the clean version, and force www -> root.

# 1. Force www -> root (non-www canonical)
https://www.executionpointconsulting.com/*   https://executionpointconsulting.com/:splat   301!

# 2. Homepage
/index.html        /        301!

# 3. Top-level pages: old .html -> clean URL
/about.html              /about              301!
/what-we-do.html         /what-we-do         301!
/industries.html         /industries         301!
/resources.html          /resources          301!
/free-ai-audit.html      /free-ai-audit      301!
/ai-audit.html           /ai-audit           301!
/privacy.html            /privacy            301!

# 4. Service pages
/services/ai-readiness-suite.html      /services/ai-readiness-suite      301!
/services/ai-strategy.html             /services/ai-strategy             301!
/services/ai-implementation.html       /services/ai-implementation       301!
/services/process-documentation.html   /services/process-documentation   301!
/services/training-enablement.html     /services/training-enablement     301!
/services/operations-retainer.html     /services/operations-retainer     301!

# 5. Industry pages
/industries/real-estate.html            /industries/real-estate            301!
/industries/insurance.html              /industries/insurance              301!
/industries/professional-services.html  /industries/professional-services  301!

# Notes:
# - One line per page is required. Netlify wildcards only match at the END
#   of a path, so a single "/*.html" rule does NOT work.
# - A rule for a .html file that doesn't exist is harmless; it just never fires.
# - If you add new pages later, add a matching line here.
